"Drudgery chests are Wright-made little factories that can be taught repetitive jobs."
"Teaching one takes about 20 examples, and it can be re-instructed for new tasks."
"Artonans seek them eagerly; orders have waiting lists and Artonans supply the materials."
"Automated process panels are a component; another component is in low supply."
"A large drudgery room can make a meal of the day that can be watched through a window."
"It cooks by mimicking its trainer: pans bounce in the trainer's rhythm, knives chop, ladles dip."
"It can cook the same meal for a week with resupply and fixes for dulling knives or drifting pans."
